    "## HAB-MAP-POLY\n",
    "\n",
    "**Habitat Map (polygon) - Mediterranean Pilot Region Version 0 (2024-03-01 - 2024-10-31)**\n",
    "\n",
    "This dataset is a predictive map of our habitats of interest (salt marsh, seagrass, mangrove) represented with polygons, in Geopackage format. Two levels of typology can be proposed: class-lv1,which corresponds to the presence of a habitat, and class-lvl2, which corresponds to a finer discrimination of our habitats into broad classes (e.g.: Seagrass densities and Salt marsh belts). The polygons are the results of a pixel-level prediction based on Sentinel 2 time series analysis through machine learning.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this Mediterranean extract, the predicted habitat is **Posidonia**, code **7**, shown in green. The polygons describe predicted meadow boundaries.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metadata | Value |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Metadata identifier | 9709c601-c0d4-446a-9d3d-c09d2563a939 |\n",
    "| Metadata date | 2026-02-06 |\n",
    "| Publication date | 2026-02-06 |\n",
    "| Metadata language / encoding | French (`fre`) / UTF-8 (`utf8`) |\n",
    "| Coordinate reference system | EPSG:3035 — ETRS89-extended / LAEA Europe |\n",
    "| Observation period | 2024-03-01 to 2024-10-31 |\n",
    "| Spatial resolution recorded in XML | 10 m |\n",
    "| Geographic bounds (longitude) | -7.229857956347076 to 10.314641151947304° |\n",
    "| Geographic bounds (latitude) | 37.30273144839746 to 42.34809245162647° |\n",
    "| Distribution format | Geopackage, version 1.0 |\n",
    "| Topic category | environment |\n",
    "| Metadata XML schema | http://www.isotc211.org/2005/gmd http://schemas.opengis.net/iso/19139/20070417/gmd/gmd.xsd |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Contacts**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Metadata contact: Cecile Curti, i-Sea — cecile.curti@i-sea.fr.\n",
    "- Resource provider: Benoit Beguet, i-Sea — benoit.beguet@i-sea.fr.\n",
    "- Resource provider: Oscar Serrano, CEAB — oserrano@ceab.csic.es.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Keywords**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Place: Mediterranean, Pilot Region Version 0.\n",
    "- Theme: Habitats and biotopes, Bio-geographical regions.\n",
    "  Thesaurus: GEMET - INSPIRE themes, version 1.0; published 2008-06-01. Identifier: `geonetwork.thesaurus.external.theme.httpinspireeceuropaeutheme-theme`. Registry address recorded in XML: `http://localhost:8080/geonetwork/srv/api/registries/vocabularies/external.theme.httpinspireeceuropaeutheme-theme`.\n",
    "- Theme: Coastal Blue Carbon, ESA, European Space Agency, i-Sea, CEAB, Habitat mapping, Satellite, EO, Earth Observation, Copernicus, Monitoring, Mediterranean Coast, Subtidal Seagrass, Posidonia.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Lineage and processing**\n",
    "\n",
    "The habitat map is produced with a machine learning process (RandomForest) using labelled reference data at the hexagonal mesh scale and Sentinel 2 time series (selected at low tide during the growing season between March and October). A specific typology was defined to exhaustively describe land cover. Reference samples were then constructed on the basis of VHR images, field observations or existing maps. Sentinel 2 images were selected and prepared, and a set of radiometric indices were then calculated and added to the information stack. A RandomForest classification model was then trained and evaluated before being applied to all image pixels. The raw prediction was vectorized, and the classes of interest were selected. Depending on the typology level of the reference data, the model is trained and applied with level2 typology the predicted classes are merged to obtain level1 typology. If level2 is not available, the model is trained and applied with level1 typology. This product has also been trained and predicted at local site level, with no validation step.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Funding, rights and attribution**\n",
    "\n",
    "This project has received funding from the European Space Agency's Earth Observation Science for Society (EO4Society) programmatic element of the ESA FutureEO-1 Segment-2 Programme, Coastal Blue Carbon project under Contract No. 4000143758/23/I-NS (c) 2024-2026, CBC Product, i-Sea, All rights reserved contains ESA Copernicus data 2024"
   ]
  },
