    "## HAB-MAP-GRID\n",
    "\n",
    "**Habitat Map Hexagonal (hexagonal mesh) - Mediterranean Pilot Region Version 0 (2024-03-01 - 2024-10-31)**\n",
    "\n",
    "This layer is a predictive map of habitats of interest (salt marsh, seagrass, mangrove) represented on a fixed hexagonal grid of 20m sides, in Geopackage format. Two levels of typology are proposed: class-lv1, which corresponds to the presence of the above-mentioned habitats, and class-lvl2, which corresponds to a finer discrimination (e.g.: seagrass densities and salt marsh vegetation communities). The hexagonal mesh is the result of a majority voting system from the pixel-level predicted and vectorized map based on Sentinel 2 time series analysis through a machine learning, proposed in the product: 'Habitat map polygon'.\n",
    "\n",
    "The grid also contains bathymetry (`mean_bathy`), classification margins (`margin_mean`, `margin_std`), and confidence (`confidence_score`, `confidence_legend`). The five confidence classes are very high, high, moderate, low and very low. Confidence is a model indicator, rather than a measured accuracy rate. The bathymetry unit and vertical datum are unspecified. The **20 m hexagon side length** describes the mesh; the XML resolution field below records **10 m**.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metadata | Value |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Metadata identifier | 51e51758-f549-4f6a-a5db-ff47b537dc28 |\n",
    "| Metadata date | 2026-02-06 |\n",
    "| Publication date | 2026-02-06 |\n",
    "| Metadata language / encoding | French (`fre`) / UTF-8 (`utf8`) |\n",
    "| Coordinate reference system | EPSG:3035 — ETRS89-extended / LAEA Europe |\n",
    "| Observation period | 2024-03-01 to 2024-10-31 |\n",
    "| Spatial resolution recorded in XML | 10 m |\n",
    "| Geographic bounds (longitude) | -7.227540379009844 to 10.315043579880012° |\n",
    "| Geographic bounds (latitude) | 37.30242537840972 to 42.34881482953961° |\n",
    "| Distribution format | Geopackage, version 1.0 |\n",
    "| Topic category | environment |\n",
    "| Metadata XML schema | http://www.isotc211.org/2005/gmd http://schemas.opengis.net/iso/19139/20070417/gmd/gmd.xsd |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Contacts**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Metadata contact: Cecile Curti, i-Sea — cecile.curti@i-sea.fr.\n",
    "- Resource provider: Benoit Beguet, i-Sea — benoit.beguet@i-sea.fr.\n",
    "- Resource provider: Oscar Serrano, CEAB — oserrano@ceab.csic.es.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Keywords**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Place: Mediterranean, Pilot Region Version 0.\n",
    "- Theme: Habitats and biotopes, Bio-geographical regions.\n",
    "  Thesaurus: GEMET - INSPIRE themes, version 1.0; published 2008-06-01. Identifier: `geonetwork.thesaurus.external.theme.httpinspireeceuropaeutheme-theme`. Registry address recorded in XML: `http://localhost:8080/geonetwork/srv/api/registries/vocabularies/external.theme.httpinspireeceuropaeutheme-theme`.\n",
    "- Theme: Coastal Blue Carbon, ESA, European Space Agency, i-Sea, CEAB, Habitat mapping, Satellite, EO, Earth Observation, Copernicus, Monitoring, Hexagonal mesh, Mediterranean Coast, Subtidal Seagrass, Posidonia.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Lineage and processing**\n",
    "\n",
    "The habitat map is produced with a machine learning process (RandomForest) using labelled reference data at the hexagonal mesh scale and Sentinel 2 time series (selected at low tide during the growing season between March and October). A specific typology was defined to exhaustively describe land cover. Reference samples were then constructed on the basis of VHR images, field observations or existing maps. Sentinel 2 images were selected and prepared, and a set of radiometric indices were then calculated and added to the information stack. A RandomForest classification model was then trained and evaluated before being applied to all image pixels. The raw prediction was vectorized, and the classes of interest were selected. Depending on the typology level of the reference data, the model is trained and applied with level2 typology the predicted classes are merged to obtain level1 typology. If level2 is not available, the model is trained and applied with level1 typology. The prediction is then adapted to the hexagonal mesh by assigning each hexagon the value of the class that covers the majority of its area. This product has also been trained and predicted at local site level, with no validation step.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Funding, rights and attribution**\n",
